spans.s:
. A. दंसति, दंसयते or दासयते, &c.,
to bite; to destroy, overpower; to see, (दंसति ?);
cl. 10. P. दंसयति, &c., to speak or to shine.

दंशक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, biting, stinging;
(अस्), m. a dog; gad-fly, common fly; N. of a
prince of Kampana; (इका), f. a kind of gad-fly.

दंष्ट्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, tusked, having tusks;
(आ), f. = दाढिका, a beard (?); a kind of plant; [cf.
नकुलेष्टा.]

दान्त 1. दान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दम्),
tamed, broken in, subdued, daunted, bridled, re-
strained; tame, mild; patient of privations or aus-
terity, &c.; resigned; liberal (fr. rt. 1. दा?); (अस्),
m. a tamed ox or steer; a donor, giver (fr. rt. 1. दा);
N. of a plant, = दमनक, = वड, = वट, Ficus
[]
Indica; N. of a son of Bhīma, king of Vidarbha;
(आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of the Atharva-veda;
(आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.

दन्तुरक, अस्, आ, अम्, having prominent teeth;
(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people living to the east of
Madhya-deśa.

दन्व् दन्व्, cl. 1. P. दन्वति, &c., to go
or move; [cf. 1. दु, धन्व्, धाव्;
Gr. δονέω = Caus. दन्वयामि.]
